# MNIST — draw on a 28x28 Skia grid; every new cell runs a small neural network
# (predict) on the UI thread, lighting the network graph and the 0-9/N/A
# prediction row; the eraser clears the grid.
# What this test covers: drawing a "1" (vertical stroke), erase; a "7" (top bar
# + diagonal), erase; a "0" as four strokes; strokes that start inside and
# leave the canvas (out-of-bounds cells must be ignored); a tap on a single
# cell; dense scribbling over the whole grid (hundreds of touched cells, so
# the surrounding-cells path and predict run with a large list); erasing
# twice in a row and erasing an empty grid.
# Grid spans x 61-341, y 437-717; the eraser is icon-only at (330,802).
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/mnist"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 10000
wait 1500
# "1"
gesture pan 201 470 0 220 900
wait 800
press 330 802
wait 600
# "7"
gesture pan 130 480 140 0 700
wait 300
gesture pan 270 480 -80 200 900
wait 800
press 330 802
wait 600
# "0" as four strokes.
gesture pan 150 480 100 0 600
wait 200
gesture pan 250 480 0 190 700
wait 200
gesture pan 250 670 -100 0 600
wait 200
gesture pan 150 670 0 -190 700
wait 800
press 330 802
wait 600
# Single cell, then strokes leaving the canvas.
press 201 577
wait 400
gesture pan 200 577 190 0 600
wait 300
gesture pan 200 577 0 230 600
wait 300
gesture pan 100 600 -90 -250 700
wait 800
press 330 802
wait 600
# Dense scribble over the whole grid.
gesture pan 70 450 260 60 600
wait 500
gesture pan 330 520 -260 60 600
wait 500
gesture pan 70 600 260 60 600
wait 500
gesture pan 330 680 -260 20 600
wait 500
gesture pan 100 445 0 265 600
wait 500
gesture pan 200 445 0 265 600
wait 500
gesture pan 300 445 0 265 600
wait 1500
press 330 802
wait 300
press 330 802
wait 300
press 330 802
wait 2500
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\" id=\"xmark\""
wait 1500
